Based on the Pomelo project details, here are the critical BOM fixes you must make before committing to KiCad:

🔧 1. SiPM Part Number (MOST CRITICAL)
❌ Incorrect: Generic "SiPM" or placeholder (e.g., "SiPM 10x10mm")
✅ Fix: Broadcom AFBR-S4N44P014M
Why: The project explicitly uses this exact model. Generic SiPMs will not work due to incompatible electrical characteristics (e.g., gain, noise, timing).
Verification: Check if your BOM lists this exact part number (not "AFBR-S4N44P014" or similar variants).
🔧 2. Scintillator Specification
❌ Incorrect: "CsI" or "CsI Crystal" (missing doping)
✅ Fix: CsI(Tl) crystal, 10mm x 10mm x 20mm
Why: Thallium-doped (Tl) is essential for gamma spectroscopy. Pure CsI has poor light yield.
Note: Do not list "CsI" alone—this is a common mistake that breaks calibration.
🔧 3. Additional BOM Checks
Component	Common Error	Correct Specification
PCB Size	Listed in BOM (e.g., "5cm x 10cm")	Remove from BOM (BOM = components only)
Calibration Sources	Included (e.g., "Am-241")	Remove (these are not part of the device)
SiPM Manufacturer	"Avago" instead of "Broadcom"	Broadcom (Avago acquired Broadcom in 2015, but part numbers remain Broadcom)
⚠️ Why These Fixes Matter
Using the wrong SiPM (e.g., Hamamatsu S12647-010) will cause no signal or poor energy resolution.
Listing "CsI" instead of "CsI(Tl)" will result in unusable calibration (no visible peaks for gamma lines).
Including PCB size/calibration sources in the BOM will confuse manufacturers.
🛠️ Before Committing to KiCad
Verify SiPM part number in your BOM → AFBR-S4N44P014M.
Replace "CsI" → "CsI(Tl) crystal, 10x10x20mm".
Delete all non-component entries (PCB size, calibration sources, etc.).
Cross-check with Broadcom's datasheet for part number validity.
💡 Pro Tip: The project creator confirmed they use AFBR-S4N44P014M (not a generic SiPM), so your BOM must reflect this. Generic SiPMs are incompatible with the signal chain design.

